     "up": {"title":"Information technology or information system? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These cases are closer calls. For each one ask: are data, people and procedures actually working with the tools for a purpose yet? If not, it is still only information technology.</p>","items":[{"t":"A cloud accounting subscription that a bakery in Bridgetown has paid for, but nobody has set up: no accounts, no data and no users yet.","bin":0,"fb":"Paid-for software with no data, users or procedures is still a tool on its own: information technology."},{"t":"The same bakery's owner enters each day's sales into that cloud package every evening, following a checklist, and her accountant reviews a monthly profit statement.","bin":1,"fb":"Now data, a user, a procedure and a purpose (the profit statement) are working with the tool: an information system."},{"t":"A fishing co-operative in Grenville, Grenada: members text their catch weights to one phone, a clerk logs them in a shared sheet each evening and the manager gets a weekly catch summary to set prices.","bin":1,"fb":"The technology is simple, but all the components work together to turn data into information for decisions. Simple tools can still form an information system."},{"t":"A brand-new patient database at a hospital in Kingston. No staff have been trained, no procedures have been written and it holds no records.","bin":0,"fb":"An empty, unused database is software and storage only. Without data, users and procedures it is not yet an information system."},{"t":"A fibre-optic cable laid between Basseterre and the airport by a telecoms company, not yet carrying any services.","bin":0,"fb":"Network hardware on its own is information technology. It becomes part of an IS only when it carries data for users and a purpose."},{"t":"The online tax portal in Georgetown, Guyana: taxpayers file returns, officers follow audit procedures and managers receive monthly compliance reports.","bin":1,"fb":"Hardware, software, data, procedures, users and a network all serve the purpose of collecting tax: an information system."},{"t":"A taxi driver's smartphone in Oranjestad, Aruba, used only to play music while driving.","bin":0,"fb":"A device used for entertainment is not turning business data into information for an organisation: information technology only."},{"t":"The same taxi firm's dispatch app: customers book rides, drivers accept jobs on their phones following the firm's rules, and the owner sees daily trips and earnings per driver.","bin":1,"fb":"Now phones, the app, booking data, drivers, rules and the mobile network work together to produce information for the owner: an information system."}],"win":"Well judged. The test is never how advanced the technology is. A simple shared sheet can be part of an information system, and an expensive new database is only IT until people, data and procedures put it to work."}
