     "up": {"title":"Operations or decisions? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These systems are at work across the region, and some use the same data for different jobs. Decide what each one is MAINLY for.</p>","items":[{"t":"At a water treatment plant in Vieux Fort, sensors measure chlorine levels and automatically adjust the dosing pumps.","bin":0,"fb":"Measuring and adjusting a physical process automatically is process control: operations."},{"t":"The finance director of a rum distillery in Barbados models how a 15 per cent rise in molasses prices would change next year's profit.","bin":1,"fb":"A what-if model for a manager's decision: a DSS, on the decision side."},{"t":"Project teams at an engineering firm in Trinidad share drawings in one online workspace and hold daily video meetings between San Fernando and Port of Spain.","bin":0,"fb":"Helping teams communicate and share work is enterprise collaboration: operations."},{"t":"A rice mill in Guyana produces a nightly list of only the drying silos whose moisture readings went out of range, for the production manager to review.","bin":1,"fb":"The readings come from process sensors, but this output is an exception report for a manager to act on: MIS, decisions."},{"t":"At the same rice mill, the dryer switches off a burner by itself when the grain temperature passes its set limit.","bin":0,"fb":"No manager is involved: the computer compares a reading with a set value and acts. That is process control, operations."},{"t":"Reservation agents at a regional airline office in St. John's, Antigua, book seats and issue e-tickets.","bin":0,"fb":"Recording bookings is routine transaction processing: operations."},{"t":"The board of a bauxite company in Jamaica views world aluminium prices beside the output of each mine on one dashboard.","bin":1,"fb":"Summarised internal data with external data for senior executives: an EIS, supporting strategic decisions."},{"t":"The director of a tourism authority in Basseterre compares five-year cruise and stay-over trends to decide which markets to advertise in.","bin":1,"fb":"Using trends to make a strategic choice is decision support, not day-to-day operations."}],"win":"Excellent. You looked past the technology to the purpose. The same sensor data can control a machine (operations) or feed a manager's exception report (decisions)."}
