     "up": {"title":"Which kind of report? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A pharmacy chain has branches in St. George's, Grenville and Gouyave, Grenada. Some of these reports look alike, so decide what each one shows and when it is produced.</p>","items":[{"t":"The monthly list of every controlled drug dispensed, with patient, prescriber and quantity, kept for the inspector.","bin":0,"fb":"Every record listed line by line: detailed."},{"t":"A weekly chart of total sales for each branch.","bin":1,"fb":"Totals per branch condense many records: summarised."},{"t":"A daily list of only the prescriptions where the dose entered is above the maximum safe dose.","bin":2,"fb":"Only records that break a limit: exception."},{"t":"The owner asks this morning, just once: \"Which branch sold the most mosquito repellent during the chikungunya scare?\"","bin":3,"fb":"A one-off question answered on request: ad hoc."},{"t":"A quarterly report showing the average waiting time at EVERY branch, compared with the 15-minute target.","bin":1,"fb":"All branches are shown with averages, so it is summarised. If it showed only branches over target, it would be an exception report."},{"t":"A quarterly report showing ONLY the branches whose average waiting time was over the 15-minute target.","bin":2,"fb":"Only the cases outside the limit appear: exception."},{"t":"A list printed every evening of each refund issued, with the time, amount and staff member.","bin":0,"fb":"Each individual refund is listed: detailed. It gives an audit trail."},{"t":"The accountant requests a one-time breakdown of card versus cash sales since the new card machines were installed.","bin":3,"fb":"Unscheduled and produced to answer a specific question: ad hoc."}],"win":"Well judged. You separated reports by how much they show (everything, totals or only exceptions) and when they are produced (scheduled or on request)."}
