     "up": {"title":"Which list does the examiner want? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"A Paper 02 question asks: \"Identify and describe TWO components of the information system at Island Breeze Hotel. (4 marks)\" Which answer would earn ALL four marks?","options":[{"t":"\"Reports: the daily occupancy report. Network: the Internet.\"","fb":"Reports are an output, not a component, and \"the Internet\" alone does not describe the hotel's network. At most one mark."},{"t":"\"Hardware and software: the computers and programs.\"","fb":"This names two components but describes neither and gives no hotel detail."},{"t":"\"Databases: they store guest information. IT professionals: they maintain the system.\"","fb":"Neither term is the syllabus word (data, users), and the descriptions are not applied to the hotel. This risks losing marks."},{"t":"\"Data: raw facts such as guests' names, room numbers and payment amounts captured at check-in and processed into occupancy information. Procedures: written instructions, such as the steps receptionists follow to cancel a booking, so that users operate the system correctly.\"","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Both use syllabus terms, say what the component is and apply it to the hotel: identify plus describe for each."}]}
