     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">The Seaside Pharmacy in Bodden Town uses a computerised system to dispense prescriptions, manage stock and accept card payments. After a hurricane, the pharmacy reopened with its computers undamaged, but the Internet connection to the card-payment provider and its suppliers was down for two weeks.</p>",
     "prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Identify the <b>six</b> components of an information system, giving an example of each from Seaside Pharmacy. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>Describe the relationship among the components of the pharmacy's information system. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>Using the stimulus, explain why the failure of one component affects the whole system. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol>",
     "min": 220,
     "max": 420,
     "frame": "<p><b>(a)</b> Hardware: ... Software: ... Data: ... Procedures: ... Users: ... Network: ...<br><b>(b)</b> Hardware depends on software because ... Software is instructions for the machine, whereas procedures ... Users follow procedures to ... Data links ... The network connects ...<br><b>(c)</b> When the network failed, ... This shows that ...</p>",
     "checklist": [
      "I named all six components (and did not list reports).",
      "I gave a pharmacy example for each.",
      "I used linking verbs: depends on, instructs, follows, connects.",
      "I contrasted software with procedures.",
      "I explained the hurricane network failure and its effect on card payments and suppliers.",
      "I stated that the system is only as strong as its weakest component."
     ],
