     "up": {"title":"Input, output or storage? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>This list includes control-system devices and some less familiar hardware. Sort each by the main function it performs in the situation described.</p>","items":[{"t":"A sensor measuring humidity in a cigar-storage room in Kingston","bin":0,"fb":"It measures a physical quantity and sends it to the computer: input."},{"t":"An actuator that opens a vent when the humidity is too high","bin":1,"fb":"It turns a computer signal into physical action: output."},{"t":"The security camera filming a hotel car park in Ocho Rios","bin":0,"fb":"It captures images: input."},{"t":"The memory card inside that camera holding the last week of footage","bin":2,"fb":"It keeps the footage when power is off: secondary storage."},{"t":"A speech-generating device used by a student who cannot speak","bin":1,"fb":"It turns selected words into speech: output."},{"t":"A magnetic tape cartridge holding last year's archived bank records","bin":2,"fb":"Large, cheap, sequential-access storage for archives."},{"t":"An MICR reader at a bank counter in Nassau","bin":0,"fb":"It reads magnetic-ink characters on cheques: input."},{"t":"A cloud storage account holding the off-site backups","bin":2,"fb":"Files kept on remote servers: storage."},{"t":"A 3D printer producing a replacement plastic part","bin":1,"fb":"It creates a physical object from the computer's data: output."},{"t":"A thermal printer producing a boarding pass","bin":1,"fb":"Hard copy from processed data: output."}],"win":"Well sorted. Sensors and cameras bring data in; actuators, printers and speech devices send results out; memory cards, tape and cloud accounts keep data for later."}
