     "up": {"title":"The right printer for the job (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"A hardware store in Basseterre prints till receipts on thermal printers. Customers complain that receipts they keep for 12-month tool warranties have faded to blank by the time a tool breaks. The store still wants fast, quiet printing at the tills. Which solution is BEST?","options":[{"t":"Replace every till printer with a dot-matrix printer, because impact printing does not fade","fb":"It would solve fading but fail the requirement for quiet printing, and ribbons need replacing."},{"t":"Keep the thermal printers for speed and quiet, and also email a digital copy of each receipt or store it on the customer's account","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. It keeps the strengths of thermal printing and removes its weakness, because a digital copy does not fade."},{"t":"Ask customers to photocopy their receipts as soon as they get home","fb":"This moves the problem onto the customer and many will forget. The store's own system should solve it."},{"t":"Replace every till printer with a laser printer","fb":"Laser printers are bulky, costly per till and need toner. It is far more than the job needs."}]}
