     "up": {"title":"CPU, GPU or motherboard? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The technician at Island Tech Repairs now gives customers symptoms and upgrade questions. Decide which processing device each one is about.</p>","items":[{"t":"A video editor's preview stutters while CPU use is only 15 per cent; upgrading this part fixes it","bin":1,"fb":"The CPU is not busy, so the graphics work is the bottleneck: the GPU."},{"t":"Researchers in Trinidad use it to train a machine-learning model because it does thousands of identical calculations in parallel","bin":1,"fb":"Massively parallel calculation is the GPU's strength, even outside graphics."},{"t":"In many cheap laptops, an integrated version is built into the same chip as the processor","bin":1,"fb":"Integrated graphics: a GPU sharing the CPU chip."},{"t":"Decides which type, and how much, RAM a PC can take","bin":2,"fb":"The RAM slots and their supported types are on the motherboard."},{"t":"Its socket decides which processors can be fitted in an upgrade","bin":2,"fb":"The CPU socket is part of the motherboard."},{"t":"Its buses carry data from the SSD into RAM when a file is opened","bin":2,"fb":"The motherboard's circuits connect storage, memory and processor."},{"t":"Decodes each instruction of the operating system and sends control signals to the other parts","bin":0,"fb":"Decoding and control are jobs of the CPU's control unit."},{"t":"Its clock speed and number of cores largely decide how fast a large spreadsheet recalculates","bin":0,"fb":"General calculation speed depends on the CPU."},{"t":"Runs the payroll program's long sequence of different calculations and comparisons","bin":0,"fb":"Varied, step-by-step instructions are general-purpose CPU work."}],"win":"Excellent. You diagnosed by function: general instructions and control point to the CPU, parallel graphics or maths to the GPU, and sockets, slots and buses to the motherboard."}
