     "up": {"title":"Inside the CPU (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A hotel in Grand Case runs its billing program. Match each part or feature of the processor to what it does. Nine pairs, including the control bus, clock speed and cores.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Control unit","r":"Decodes each instruction and sends the timing signals that coordinate the whole cycle"},{"l":"Arithmetic logic unit (ALU)","r":"Decides whether a guest's bill is greater than her credit limit"},{"l":"Program counter","r":"Is increased after each fetch so the CPU knows where the next instruction is"},{"l":"Accumulator","r":"Temporarily holds the result of the latest calculation inside the CPU"},{"l":"Control bus","r":"Carries the \"read\" or \"write\" signal that tells memory what to do"},{"l":"Address bus","r":"Carries the memory location the CPU wants to read from or write to"},{"l":"Data bus","r":"Carries the actual value between memory and the CPU"},{"l":"Clock speed","r":"Measured in gigahertz: how many cycles the CPU completes each second"},{"l":"Multiple cores","r":"Let the processor run instructions from two programs at the same moment"}],"win":"Well matched. You can explain each part's role and the features that make one processor faster than another."}
