     "win": "Excellent. RAM holds data temporarily during processing; secondary storage is permanent and may be internal, external or removable; flash drives and cards make handy backups; and with no storage at all a computer is a dumb terminal.",
     "tutor": [
      {
       "h": "Temporary or permanent?",
       "p": "<p>RAM is primary storage: it holds data <b>during processing</b> and loses it without power. Hard drives, SSDs and flash drives keep data permanently.</p>"
      },
      {
       "h": "Inside, in its own case, or carried?",
       "p": "<p>Inside the system unit = <b>internal</b>. In its own case on a cable = <b>external</b>. A medium you take out and carry = <b>removable</b>.</p>"
      }
     ],
