     "up": {"title":"Which translator fits? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These descriptions give consequences and clues rather than names. Work out which translator must be at work in each case.</p>","main":"Which language translator does this evidence point to?","bins":["Compiler","Interpreter","Assembler"],"items":[{"t":"An error on line 40 is not discovered until lines 1 to 39 have already run and produced output","bin":1,"fb":"An interpreter translates and executes as it goes, so it meets the error only when it reaches that line."},{"t":"Each mnemonic is replaced by the binary op code for one particular microcontroller","bin":2,"fb":"A one-to-one translation from assembly language: an assembler."},{"t":"Firmware for a card terminal is written in a low-level language with one instruction per machine operation","bin":2,"fb":"Low-level, one-to-one code for hardware: an assembler."},{"t":"Translation takes several minutes, but afterwards the program runs again and again with no further translation","bin":0,"fb":"Whole-program translation done once, then fast repeated runs: a compiler."},{"t":"The program will not run on the client's PC unless the translator is also installed there","bin":1,"fb":"An interpreter must be present every time the program runs."},{"t":"A programmer writes MOV and JMP instructions to control the motor of an automatic gate in Oranjestad","bin":2,"fb":"Mnemonics for one processor are translated by an assembler."},{"t":"The finished payroll program must be re-translated separately before it can run on a different type of processor","bin":0,"fb":"A compiled executable is tied to one platform, so the source must be compiled again."},{"t":"A tutor types a single command and sees its result immediately, then types the next","bin":1,"fb":"Translate and run one statement at a time: an interpreter."},{"t":"A games studio in Kingston sells its program to customers without ever releasing the source code","bin":0,"fb":"Only a compiler produces a stand-alone executable that can be distributed without the source code."}],"win":"Excellent analysis. Stand-alone executables, slow translation then fast runs and platform-specific output point to a compiler; needing the translator at run time and meeting errors only when reached point to an interpreter; low-level mnemonics point to an assembler."}
