     "up": {"title":"Operating system, translator or utility? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>All of these are system software, and the descriptions are more technical than before. Decide which branch each belongs to.</p>","main":"Operating system, language translator or utility?","bins":["Operating system","Language translator","Utility"],"items":[{"t":"Loads the correct driver when a card reader is plugged in","bin":0,"fb":"Device management through drivers is an OS function."},{"t":"Rearranges file fragments on an HDD into continuous blocks","bin":2,"fb":"A disk defragmenter is a utility."},{"t":"Moves part of a program out of RAM into virtual memory on the drive","bin":0,"fb":"Virtual memory is part of the OS's memory management."},{"t":"Converts MOV and ADD into op codes for a microcontroller","bin":1,"fb":"An assembler."},{"t":"Prevents one running program from writing into memory used by another","bin":0,"fb":"Protecting memory is part of the OS's memory management."},{"t":"Removes 15 GB of temporary files","bin":2,"fb":"Disk clean-up is a utility."},{"t":"Translates and runs a script one statement at a time, stopping at line 22","bin":1,"fb":"An interpreter."},{"t":"Decides how long each running program may use the CPU before switching to the next","bin":0,"fb":"Scheduling is the OS's process management."},{"t":"Restores a deleted folder from last night's copy","bin":2,"fb":"Backup and recovery is a utility."},{"t":"Scans incoming email attachments for malicious code","bin":2,"fb":"Antivirus is a utility."},{"t":"Holds print jobs from five users in a queue on the disk and sends them to the printer in turn","bin":0,"fb":"Spooling is part of the OS's device management."},{"t":"Lists every syntax error in a payroll program only after translating the whole file","bin":1,"fb":"Whole-program translation with errors listed at the end: a compiler."}],"win":"Excellent. The OS manages resources continuously, translators convert code into machine code, and utilities do specific maintenance or protection jobs when they run."}
