     "up": {"title":"Monitoring or control? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"In an automated greenhouse in Soufrière, St. Lucia, sensors measure humidity. When humidity drops below 60 per cent, the system switches on misters until it reaches 75 per cent. It also emails the farmer a daily log of readings. Which statement is MOST accurate?","options":[{"t":"It is a monitoring system, because it records readings and emails a log to the farmer","fb":"The emailed log is a monitoring feature, but the system also acts on humidity through the misters, so \"monitoring\" alone is incomplete."},{"t":"It is a control system, because the misters act on the humidity using feedback; the daily log is an extra monitoring feature","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The computer changes the process through an actuator and checks the new readings, which is control. Real devices often add monitoring features such as logs and alerts."},{"t":"It is a control system, because it has a humidity sensor","fb":"Having a sensor does not make it control; monitoring systems have sensors too. The reason is the actuator and feedback."},{"t":"It is not an embedded system, because it sends email over a network","fb":"Network connection does not stop a device being an embedded system; it is still a dedicated computer inside the greenhouse equipment."}]}
