     "up": {"title":"Equip a new office in Cole Bay (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Harbour View Accounting has grown to ten staff and now serves clients in Sint Maarten and Anguilla. You are its IT consultant. Each decision builds on the last, and some choices are partly right.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p>A large payroll client has employees on both islands, but the firm's off-the-shelf payroll package does not handle Anguilla's deductions. What do you recommend?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Do the Anguilla payroll by hand in a spreadsheet each month.","to":"bad1","fb":"Manual calculations for many employees invite errors and penalties."},{"t":"Commission a programmer to write a completely new bespoke payroll system.","to":"ok1","fb":"It would fit exactly, but it costs far more, takes months and must be maintained by the firm."},{"t":"Ask the vendor for its Anguilla module, or have the package customised, keeping the tested core of the software.","to":"n2","fb":"Good. Customising proven software meets the special need at lower cost and risk than starting again."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p>Two partners now travel between the islands every week and work on client files on the ferry and in clients' offices. Which computers do you choose for them?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Powerful desktop towers with large hard disks, so they never run out of space.","to":"bad2","fb":"Desktops cannot travel, and magnetic disks are more easily damaged."},{"t":"Light laptops with a multi-core processor, 16 GB of RAM, an SSD and full-disk encryption switched on.","to":"n3","fb":"Right. Portability, enough power for the accounting package, a robust SSD and encryption in case a laptop is lost."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p>The office installs a smart door lock and two CCTV cameras that connect to the office Wi-Fi. The installer leaves them on their factory settings. What do you do?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Change the default passwords, put the devices on a separate network from client data, and check how long the maker will supply firmware updates.","to":"n4","fb":"Excellent. These are embedded systems: reachable once connected and hard to update, so isolate them and remove the easy way in."},{"t":"Leave the factory settings; locks and cameras do not hold client data.","to":"bad3","fb":"An unprotected device on the same network gives an attacker a route to everything else."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p>Finally, the partners ask how client records should be backed up before hurricane season.</p>","choices":[{"t":"An automatic nightly encrypted backup to cloud storage, plus a weekly encrypted external drive kept on the other island, with a test restore every quarter.","to":"good","fb":"Excellent. Several copies, on different media, one off-site, and tested so you know they work."},{"t":"A backup utility that copies everything nightly to a second hard disk inside the main office PC.","to":"ok2","fb":"Better than nothing, but both copies sit in one machine in one building."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Well advised.</b> The firm has software that fits both islands, portable and secure hardware, protected embedded devices and backups that would survive a storm. In Paper 02, justify each recommendation by linking a feature to a need in the stimulus.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>It works, eventually.</b> The bespoke system arrives seven months late and well over budget, and the firm now depends on one programmer to maintain it. Customising tested software would have met the need sooner and more cheaply. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok2":{"text":"<p><b>Partly protected.</b> The second disk survives a single drive failure, but a flood, fire, theft or ransomware attack on the office would destroy both copies. Try again and plan an off-site, tested copy.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Penalties.</b> A spreadsheet formula error under-deducts tax for three months and the client is fined. Try again and look for a way to extend the payroll package.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>Stuck at the office.</b> The partners cannot work while travelling, and one tower's hard disk fails after a move. Try again and match the hardware to how it will be used.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Breached.</b> An attacker logs in to a camera with its published default password and uses it to reach the file server. Try again and secure the embedded devices.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
