     "type": "write",
     "title": "Interview findings: software in a Road Town office",
     "genre": "Paper 02 structured response: types and functions of software (15 marks)",
     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">A CAPE student interviewed Ms. Romney, office administrator at the Road Harbour Realty in Road Town. Extract from the notes:<br><br>\"I write tenancy letters and send newsletters using our word processor, and I keep rent records in a spreadsheet. Our tenants pay through a property-management package that many estate agents use. The laptops run Windows; I log in each morning and I save everything in a folder called Clients. Last month the computer said the disk was full, and the technician ran something to delete temporary files. We copy the rent spreadsheet onto a flash drive on Fridays, when I remember. After Irma, the old office lost two years of records.\"</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>Use the interview extract to answer all parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Identify TWO application programs mentioned and classify each as general-purpose or special-purpose, giving a reason. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Describe TWO functions of the operating system that Ms. Romney relies on, with evidence from the extract. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Explain the role of utility software in this office, referring to TWO utilities. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Recommend ONE better tool or practice for the office's data, and justify your recommendation. <i>(4 marks)</i></li></ol>",
     "min": 200,
     "max": 400,
     "frame": "<p><b>(a)</b> The word processor is ... software because ... The property-management package is ... because ...<br><b>(b)</b> One OS function is ... The extract shows this when ... A second function is ...<br><b>(c)</b> Utilities ... For example, the disk clean-up utility ... A backup utility ...<br><b>(d)</b> I recommend ... because ... This would ... unlike the current practice of ...</p>",
