     "up": {"title":"Name the interface type (part 1) (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These cards are harder: some menus are text only, some forms contain menus, and some menus sit inside a GUI. Sort each by the type of HCI it MAINLY shows.</p>","main":"Which type of HCI is this MAINLY?","bins":["Command line","Menu","Forms","GUI"],"items":[{"t":"A customer registration screen whose Parish box is a drop-down list and whose phone box rejects letters","bin":2,"fb":"It contains a small menu, but its purpose is collecting several items of data: forms."},{"t":"A TV remote opens Settings, then Picture, then Brightness, each choice opening a further list","bin":1,"fb":"A hierarchical menu."},{"t":"Several documents open side by side, each in its own frame, with a pointer moving between them","bin":3,"fb":"Windows and a pointer: GUI."},{"t":"A text-only screen at a credit union lists \"1 Deposits 2 Loans 3 Exit\" and waits for a number","bin":1,"fb":"Text only, but the user selects from displayed options: menu."},{"t":"A user types \"ls -l\" in a terminal and gets a text listing of files","bin":0,"fb":"Command line."},{"t":"A tax portal page with boxes for taxpayer number, income and deductions, a date picker and a Submit button","bin":2,"fb":"Several labelled fields for data entry: forms."},{"t":"At the prompt \"Router#\", a technician types \"show ip interface brief\"","bin":0,"fb":"An exact command typed from memory: command line."},{"t":"Right-clicking a file shows Copy, Rename and Delete beside the pointer","bin":1,"fb":"A pop-up (context) menu: the user picks one action from a list."},{"t":"A saved script of commands archives the ledger every night","bin":0,"fb":"Scripts of typed commands belong to the command line."},{"t":"The whole desktop of resizable windows, a taskbar and icons","bin":3,"fb":"The overall environment of windows, icons, menus and pointer: GUI."}],"win":"Excellent. You decided by how the user gives instructions and what the screen is for: typed commands, a choice from a list, data entered into fields, or the whole windowed environment."}
