     "up": {"title":"Choose the right interface for the user (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Each user's situation has more than one tempting answer. Choose the interface that suits them BEST, thinking about expertise, task, setting and any limitation.</p>","items":[{"text":"A clerk at a bank in Kingston keys in 400 cheque details a day, and supervisors want consistent, validated data.","options":["forms with drop-down lists and validation","natural language","direct manipulation","speech"],"answer":0,"fb":"High-volume structured data entry needs labelled fields and validation: forms."},{"text":"A blind accountant in Bridgetown must review spreadsheets every day.","options":["a GUI with larger icons","speech output from a screen reader, with keyboard shortcuts","direct manipulation on a touchscreen","a menu with colour coding"],"answer":1,"fb":"Speech synthesis reads the content aloud, and keyboard shortcuts replace the pointer; the other choices still rely on sight."},{"text":"A laboratory technician in Port of Spain must run the same analysis on 2,000 sample files tonight.","options":["menu","forms","command line with a script","direct manipulation"],"answer":2,"fb":"An expert with a large repetitive task gains most from scripting."},{"text":"Tourists at a visitor kiosk in Castries speak many languages and stay only a minute.","options":["natural language typed in English","a GUI with icons and short labels","a command line","speech"],"answer":1,"fb":"Icons are language independent and quick to recognise; English-only text and speech exclude many visitors, and speech struggles in a busy terminal."},{"text":"A surgeon in a Georgetown operating theatre needs to call up an X-ray without touching anything.","options":["direct manipulation","speech","forms","menu on a touchscreen"],"answer":1,"fb":"Speech is hands-free, which keeps the surgeon's gloves sterile."},{"text":"A utility in Jamaica wants customers to report faults in their own words, but many customers use Creole expressions. Which is the BEST evaluation?","options":["Speech and natural language are the same, so either will work","Natural language understands every dialect automatically","Natural language could suit them, but it must be trained and tested on local expressions or it will misunderstand","A command line would be clearer for customers"],"answer":2,"fb":"Natural language removes the need to learn commands, but its key weakness is misinterpretation, especially of dialects it was not built for."},{"text":"Workers on a noisy factory floor at Point Lisas wear thick gloves.","options":["a command line","natural language typed on a keyboard","a touchscreen menu with large buttons","speech"],"answer":2,"fb":"Noise rules out speech, and gloves rule out typing; large buttons in a menu let workers recognise and press options."}],"win":"Strong evaluation. You weighed the user, the task and the setting together, and you rejected answers that ignored a limitation such as noise, sight or language."}
