      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> (i) <b>GUI</b> (graphical user interface). (ii) <b>Direct manipulation</b>. (iv) <b>Menu</b>. (v) <b>Forms</b>.</p><p><b>(b)</b> Saying \"Call home\" is a <b>speech</b> interface because the driver <b>speaks</b> the instruction and the car uses speech recognition to carry it out.</p><p><b>(c)</b> (i) The technician uses a <b>command line</b> interface. (ii) It suits him because he is an <b>expert</b> who knows the exact commands, so he can check faults quickly and with precise control.</p>",
      "teacherTip": "<p>This dial-down uses the same dashboard but gives students the list of interface types and asks for one feature at a time. Once a student is secure, return to the full version, where they must explain the difference between speech and natural language and contrast the command line with the GUI using \"whereas\".</p>"
