     "up": {"title":"Which criterion matters most here? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>For each setting, choose the principle that should carry the MOST weight and the reason that justifies it.</p>","items":[{"text":"An alarm panel in an intensive-care unit in Kingston that warns staff of a patient emergency.","options":["Use of colour backed by sound and text, because alerts must be noticed instantly and not rely on colour alone","Alignment, because the panel should look tidy","Ease of learning, because new nurses join each year"],"answer":0,"fb":"Alerts must be impossible to miss and understood by every staff member, including those with colour-vision deficiency."},{"text":"A voter-registration kiosk in Belize used once every few years by members of the public.","options":["Ease of use for experts, because staff will help","Ease of learning, because users are untrained and occasional","Use of colour, because it should look official"],"answer":1,"fb":"Occasional public users must succeed with no training."},{"text":"A data-entry screen used eight hours a day by experienced customs clerks in Port of Spain.","options":["Ease of use, because trained users need speed and few steps over many repetitions","Ease of learning, because forms must be simple","Use of colour, because clerks look at it all day"],"answer":0,"fb":"Small savings per task add up over thousands of entries for expert users."},{"text":"A government website with 3,000 pages of services.","options":["Alignment, because pages should share a grid","Ease of navigation, because users need search, clear menus and breadcrumbs to find one service among thousands","Ease of use for experts"],"answer":1,"fb":"With so much content, finding the right page is the main challenge."},{"text":"A speech-only telephone banking line.","options":["Ease of navigation, because spoken menus must stay short and clear when callers cannot see the options","Alignment, because spoken items must line up","Use of colour, because the brand matters"],"answer":0,"fb":"Alignment and colour do not apply to speech; short, clear spoken menus are essential."}],"win":"Good weighting. The justification matters as much as the choice: occasional users need learnability, heavy users need ease of use, large sites need navigation, and alerts need colour backed by sound and text."}
