     "up": {"title":"Which IT role? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"After a phishing email tricked a clerk, an insurance company in Trinidad needs one person to find which systems the attacker reached, close the weaknesses and recommend controls to stop it happening again. A second person must restore the damaged customer database from backups and check that the records are complete. Which pair of IT professionals is MOST appropriate?","options":[{"t":"IT consultant, then technical support officer","fb":"A consultant could advise, but an urgent breach investigation needs the specialist; a support officer fixes users' hardware and software problems, not databases."},{"t":"Information systems manager, then web developer","fb":"The IS manager oversees the department and would assign the work; a web developer builds websites and is not responsible for restoring the customer database."},{"t":"Information security specialist, then database administrator","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The security specialist analyses where the breach occurred and strengthens defences; the DBA protects the data's integrity and restores it from backups."},{"t":"Network engineer, then systems analyst","fb":"A network engineer keeps the network available, but tracing a breach is the security specialist's role; an analyst specifies new systems and does not restore databases."}]}
