     "up": {"title":"Which characteristic does this adaptation serve? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A regional government portal is adding features. Sort each by the user characteristic it MAINLY addresses. Some could seem to fit two bins, so decide which is the main reason.</p>","main":"Which user characteristic is this MAINLY for?","bins":["Age","Education","Disability","Cultural differences"],"items":[{"t":"Switch access for a user who can move only one finger","bin":2,"fb":"Addresses limited mobility: disability."},{"t":"Locked-down settings and picture buttons in a primary-school reading app","bin":0,"fb":"Designed for young children: age."},{"t":"Patterns as well as colours on charts for a user with colour-vision deficiency","bin":2,"fb":"Addresses a visual impairment: disability."},{"t":"Voice messages instead of text for farmers with limited reading skills in Guyana's interior","bin":1,"fb":"Addresses literacy level: education."},{"t":"Avoiding white as the main colour on a condolence-message service, because some communities link white with mourning","bin":3,"fb":"The meaning of colour varies between cultures."},{"t":"Prices shown in Caribbean guilders, US dollars or euros, as the visitor chooses","bin":3,"fb":"Currency format is a cultural difference."},{"t":"Slower time-outs and no hidden swipe gestures in the retirees' mode","bin":0,"fb":"Addresses age-related speed and familiarity: age."},{"t":"Advanced settings hidden until a user switches on \"expert mode\"","bin":1,"fb":"Matches the interface to technical knowledge: education."},{"t":"A mirrored layout for visitors who read Arabic","bin":3,"fb":"Reading direction differs between cultures and languages."},{"t":"Replacing \"Initiate remittance\" with \"Pay bill\"","bin":1,"fb":"Plain language for users with less technical vocabulary: education."}],"win":"Well sorted. You identified the main characteristic behind each adaptation, including the less obvious cultural ones: currency, reading direction and the meaning of colour."}
