     "genre": "Paper 02 structured response: evaluating HCI against criteria (15 marks)",
     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">The Harbourview Café on the Hastings boardwalk is choosing between two ordering systems. <b>System A</b> is a touchscreen GUI tablet at each table, with picture buttons, a top navigation bar for Drinks, Mains and Desserts, and orange text on a yellow background. <b>System B</b> is a staff-only POS where servers type short item codes (for example JC2 for two johnnycakes) at a terminal behind the counter. Customers are mainly cruise passengers who visit once; servers are a mix of long-serving staff and new seasonal workers.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>(a) State what is meant by \"ease of learning\" and \"ease of navigation\". <i>(2 marks)</i></p><p>(b) Evaluate System A and System B using <b>four</b> of the principles: ease of use, ease of learning, ease of navigation, alignment, use of colour. <i>(9 marks)</i></p><p>(c) Recommend which system the café should adopt, justifying your answer with reference to its users, and suggest <b>one</b> improvement to the system you recommend. <i>(4 marks)</i></p>",
