      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Ease of learning is how quickly a new user can become able to use an interface without training or help.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> System A is easier to learn because its picture buttons let a first-time customer recognise dishes instead of memorising codes like JC2.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> One problem is that orange text on a yellow background has low contrast. This means customers find the menu hard to read in bright sunlight on the boardwalk.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> The café should choose System A because its customers are cruise passengers who visit only once and need an interface they can learn instantly, and new seasonal servers would not have to memorise codes.</p>",
      "teacherTip": "<p>Use this dial-down with students who cannot yet structure a full evaluation. Once they succeed, ask them to add the same point for System B, which builds towards the comparison needed in the full question.</p>"
