     "up": {"title":"Mobile networks and VPNs: match the feature (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These descriptions explain why each feature matters rather than simply naming it. Match each term to the description that fits it.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Cell","r":"A coverage area that lets the same frequencies be reused by towers far enough apart"},{"l":"Base station","r":"Equipment that needs backup generators so a district keeps service when the power grid fails after a storm"},{"l":"Hand-over","r":"Transfers a live call between towers as a minibus travels from Five Cays to Providenciales"},{"l":"2G","r":"Enough for SMS payment alerts on a basic phone, but not for streaming"},{"l":"3G","r":"First brought mobile Internet to phones, but struggles with high-definition video"},{"l":"4G (LTE)","r":"Broadband-speed mobile data that made streaming and video apps on phones practical"},{"l":"5G","r":"Very low delay, suited to thousands of sensors working together at a smart port"},{"l":"VPN","r":"Lets a nurse on a hotel's public Wi-Fi reach the clinic's server without other guests reading her data"}],"win":"Excellent. You linked each term to its purpose: cells reuse frequencies, base stations need resilience, hand-over keeps calls alive, each generation adds speed or lower delay, and a VPN protects data across public networks."}
