     "up": {"title":"Client-server or peer-to-peer? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These clues are indirect. Decide which configuration each description points to.</p>","main":"Which configuration does this evidence point to?","bins":["Client-server","Peer-to-peer"],"items":[{"t":"One nightly backup of a single machine protects everyone's work","bin":0,"fb":"Data is stored centrally: client-server."},{"t":"When Maria's PC is switched off, nobody can open the price list stored on it","bin":1,"fb":"Shared files live on individual peers: peer-to-peer."},{"t":"Each machine shares its own printer and also uses files stored on the others","bin":1,"fb":"Every computer is both provider and user: peer-to-peer."},{"t":"Permissions must be set separately on every computer that shares a folder","bin":1,"fb":"Decentralised control: peer-to-peer."},{"t":"A dedicated machine runs a network operating system and does no one's personal work","bin":0,"fb":"A dedicated server: client-server."},{"t":"Staff log in once and the same account works on any PC in the building","bin":0,"fb":"Central accounts held on a server: client-server."},{"t":"Set-up was cheap: no server hardware and no administrator","bin":1,"fb":"Low cost with no server: peer-to-peer."},{"t":"Students at a study group swap notes directly between their laptops with a file-sharing app","bin":1,"fb":"Direct exchange between equals: peer-to-peer."},{"t":"Adding the 60th user needs only one new account, not changes on every PC","bin":0,"fb":"Central administration scales easily: client-server."},{"t":"A web browser requests a page and a web server sends it back","bin":0,"fb":"The web itself is a client-server system."}],"win":"Well reasoned. Central accounts, storage and backups point to client-server; equal machines with scattered files and permissions point to peer-to-peer."}
