     "up": {"title":"Wired or wireless? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These statements describe trade-offs rather than technologies. Decide whether each describes wired (guided) or wireless (unguided) transmission.</p>","main":"Wired or wireless?","bins":["Wired (guided)","Wireless (unguided)"],"items":[{"t":"Speed is shared among every device connected to the same access point","bin":1,"fb":"Wi-Fi bandwidth is shared."},{"t":"Unaffected by electrical interference because it carries light","bin":0,"fb":"Fibre-optic cable."},{"t":"Relaying signals through orbit adds a noticeable delay to video calls","bin":1,"fb":"Satellite links are wireless."},{"t":"Carries most of an island's international traffic along the sea bed","bin":0,"fb":"Submarine fibre-optic cables are guided media."},{"t":"A fake network with a convincing name could trick users into connecting","bin":1,"fb":"An evil-twin hotspot is a wireless threat."},{"t":"Gives each desk a steady, dedicated connection to the switch","bin":0,"fb":"A dedicated cable is a wired advantage."},{"t":"Installing it in a 200-year-old stone building in Willemstad means drilling through thick walls","bin":0,"fb":"The cost of laying cable in old buildings is a disadvantage of wired media."},{"t":"Signals can be picked up from the car park outside the building","bin":1,"fb":"Radio signals spread beyond the walls."},{"t":"Needs a clear line of sight between dishes on two hills","bin":1,"fb":"Microwave links are wireless."},{"t":"Each run is limited to about 100 m before the signal needs boosting","bin":0,"fb":"Twisted-pair Ethernet's distance limit."}],"win":"Well analysed. Wired media win on speed, stability, distance (fibre) and security; wireless media win on mobility and installation, at the cost of shared bandwidth, interference and easier interception."}
