     "up": {"title":"Which communication mode? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These situations are less familiar. Ask two questions each time: can data flow both ways, and if so, at the same time?</p>","items":[{"text":"A hub-based Ethernet LAN where each device must wait until the cable is free before sending.","options":["Half duplex","Full duplex","Simplex"],"answer":0,"fb":"Both directions, but devices take turns: half duplex."},{"text":"Switched Ethernet where a PC sends a file and receives an email at the same moment.","options":["Half duplex","Full duplex","Simplex"],"answer":1,"fb":"Simultaneous two-way traffic: full duplex."},{"text":"A GPS receiver in a taxi picks up satellite signals but never transmits.","options":["Half duplex","Full duplex","Simplex"],"answer":2,"fb":"One direction only: simplex."},{"text":"A ship's VHF radio, where each speaker says \"over\" before the other replies.","options":["Full duplex","Half duplex","Simplex"],"answer":1,"fb":"Turn-taking on one channel: half duplex."},{"text":"A link where each direction has its own capacity, so total throughput can double.","options":["Simplex","Half duplex","Full duplex"],"answer":2,"fb":"Separate capacity in each direction: full duplex."},{"text":"A rain-gauge sensor sends readings to a weather station and never receives anything back.","options":["Full duplex","Simplex","Half duplex"],"answer":1,"fb":"One-way: simplex."},{"text":"A push-to-talk intercom between a hotel's front desk and its pool bar.","options":["Simplex","Full duplex","Half duplex"],"answer":2,"fb":"Two-way, but only one person can talk at a time: half duplex."}],"win":"Excellent. Direction and timing decide the mode, whatever the technology: one way is simplex, turn-taking is half duplex and simultaneous two-way is full duplex."}
