     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">Island Breeze Hotels group has a hotel in Rodney Bay, St. Lucia, and another in Anguilla. Each hotel has about 40 staff computers, card-key systems and a guest Wi-Fi hotspot. Head office in Castries wants staff in both hotels to share booking records, managers to work from home during the hurricane season, and the group's food suppliers to log in to see orders. Weekly management meetings currently require managers to travel between the islands.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>(a) Distinguish between a LAN and a WAN, using the Island Breeze Hotels group to illustrate each. <i>(3 marks)</i></p><p>(b) Explain the function of a <b>switch</b> and a <b>router</b> in the group's network. <i>(4 marks)</i></p><p>(c) Explain how the group could use an <b>intranet</b> and an <b>extranet</b>. <i>(2 marks)</i></p><p>(d) Explain how a <b>firewall</b> and a <b>VPN</b> would protect the network when managers telecommute. <i>(4 marks)</i></p><p>(e) Explain why videoconferencing needs a <b>duplex</b> connection with high bandwidth. <i>(2 marks)</i></p>",
     "min": 300,
