      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> (i) A LAN is the network inside one hotel, for example the 40 staff computers in the Rodney Bay hotel. (ii) A WAN is the network linking the Rodney Bay hotel, the Anguilla hotel and head office in Castries across the islands.</p><p><b>(b)</b> A switch sends data only to the intended computer, using its MAC address. A router connects different networks, such as the hotel LAN and the Internet, using IP addresses.</p><p><b>(c)</b> The intranet would be used by hotel staff to share booking records. The extranet would be used by the food suppliers to log in and see orders.</p><p><b>(d)</b> A firewall filters traffic between the hotel network and the Internet and blocks unauthorised access. A VPN encrypts the manager's connection over the Internet so intercepted data cannot be read.</p><p><b>(e)</b> Videoconferencing needs duplex because the managers must speak and hear each other at the same time. It needs high bandwidth because live video sends a large amount of data per second, and too little capacity makes the picture freeze.</p>",
