     "up": {"title":"Which OSI layer is at work? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These events are less obvious than before. For each one, choose the OSI layer doing the job.</p>","items":[{"text":"A server converts a page's Unicode text into the character format the client expects.","options":["Presentation","Application","Transport","Session"],"answer":0,"fb":"Translation between data formats is a Presentation-layer job."},{"text":"TCP's three-way handshake opens a connection to port 443.","options":["Transport","Session","Network","Data Link"],"answer":0,"fb":"Handshakes, TCP and port numbers belong to the Transport layer."},{"text":"ICMP echo replies show that a ping reached the server.","options":["Network","Physical","Application","Transport"],"answer":0,"fb":"ICMP works alongside IP at the Network layer."},{"text":"A NIC adds a checksum trailer so the next switch can detect a corrupted frame.","options":["Physical","Transport","Network","Data Link"],"answer":3,"fb":"Frames and error detection by checksum belong to the Data Link layer."},{"text":"A standard defines the RJ45 pin layout and the voltages on the cable.","options":["Network","Physical","Data Link","Presentation"],"answer":1,"fb":"Connectors, pins and voltages are Physical-layer specifications."},{"text":"DNS returns the IP address for a newspaper's domain name.","options":["Transport","Network","Application","Session"],"answer":2,"fb":"DNS is an Application-layer service, even though its answer is an IP address."},{"text":"Dialogue control keeps two programs' conversation separate from others and decides whose turn it is to send.","options":["Presentation","Application","Session","Transport"],"answer":2,"fb":"Managing the dialogue is the Session layer's role."},{"text":"A repeater regenerates a weak signal halfway along a long cable.","options":["Physical","Transport","Data Link","Network"],"answer":0,"fb":"A repeater handles raw signals, not addresses: Physical layer."}],"win":"Excellent. You identified layers from their less familiar jobs: format translation, handshakes, ICMP, checksums, connectors, name lookup, dialogue control and signal regeneration."}
