     "up": {"title":"Choosing the transport protocol (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"A bank in Kingston launches an app that lets a customer hold a live video chat with a loan adviser and then upload the signed loan agreement during the same call. Which choice of transport protocols is BEST?","options":[{"t":"UDP for the live video and TCP for the signed agreement","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Each stream gets the protocol that fits it: minimal delay for live video, guaranteed complete delivery for the document."},{"t":"UDP for both, because speed matters most","fb":"Speed suits the video, but a signed agreement must arrive complete and in order; lost data in the document would not be resent."},{"t":"TCP for both, because reliability matters most","fb":"Reliability suits the document, but resending lost video data would cause lag and frozen pictures in the live chat."},{"t":"TCP for the live video and UDP for the signed agreement","fb":"This reverses the needs: the video would lag while the document could arrive incomplete."}]}
