     "up": {"title":"Wired or wireless security? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Saba Island Library's security plan has more advanced measures. Sort each by whether it mainly protects the wired network or the wireless network.</p>","main":"Which part of the network does this measure mainly protect?","bins":["Wired security","Wireless security"],"items":[{"t":"Port security shuts a switch port when an unknown laptop is plugged in","bin":0,"fb":"Controls cabled connections at the switch."},{"t":"The SAE handshake prevents offline password guessing","bin":1,"fb":"SAE is part of WPA3 Wi-Fi."},{"t":"The Wi-Fi key is changed when a staff member leaves","bin":1,"fb":"The network key controls who joins the Wi-Fi."},{"t":"MAC filtering is applied to the staff SSID","bin":1,"fb":"Filtering at the access point for wireless devices."},{"t":"The patch panel and switch are kept in a locked room","bin":0,"fb":"Physical security for cabled equipment."},{"t":"WPA2/WPA3 transitional mode is chosen for older tablets","bin":1,"fb":"A Wi-Fi encryption setting."},{"t":"Labelled cable runs are kept inside ceiling trunking","bin":0,"fb":"Protects cables from tapping and damage."},{"t":"Guest Wi-Fi is isolated so visitors cannot reach the file server","bin":1,"fb":"Separating wireless guests protects the LAN from the Wi-Fi side."},{"t":"The SSID is renamed so it does not reveal the router's model","bin":1,"fb":"The SSID is a wireless setting."},{"t":"The network socket in an empty meeting room is disabled","bin":0,"fb":"Disabling unused wired ports."}],"win":"Well sorted. Wired measures are physical and port-based; wireless measures concern the SSID, encryption, keys, isolation and filtering at the access point."}
