     "up": {"title":"Order the design process (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Put the seven stages of designing a simple network in order, from first to last.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Identify the users, devices, locations and requirements, including guest access."},{"t":"Choose the devices and media, and justify each against a requirement."},{"t":"Draw the tiers from the top: WAN cloud, router, firewall, then switch."},{"t":"Connect the end devices: solid lines for cables, dashed lines for wireless links."},{"t":"Label every device and connection, mark the LAN boundary and add a key."},{"t":"Annotate the wireless, wired and router security measures."},{"t":"Check the design: firewall at the WAN-LAN boundary, copper runs under 100 m, every device labelled."}],"win":"Correct. Requirements and justified choices come first, the diagram is built tier by tier, then labelled, secured and checked."}
