     "up": {"title":"Reading a design (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"A diagram for Dominica Coffee Exporters shows, from top to bottom: cloud, switch, brick wall, router, then the office PCs connected to the router. What is the MAIN error, and why does it matter?","options":[{"t":"The devices are in the wrong order: it should be cloud, router, firewall, switch, PCs, so the router joins the WAN, all WAN-LAN traffic is filtered and the switch serves the PCs","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. As drawn, the switch faces the Internet and the PCs hang off the router, which shows a misunderstanding of what each device does."},{"t":"The brick wall should be drawn as a cloud, because the firewall is part of the Internet","fb":"The brick wall is the correct firewall symbol; the problem is where the devices are placed."},{"t":"Nothing is wrong, because every required device is present","fb":"Having the right devices is not enough; their order determines how traffic flows and whether it is filtered."},{"t":"The PCs should connect straight to the cloud for speed","fb":"That would bypass the router and firewall entirely, leaving every PC exposed."}]}
