     "up": {"title":"Pick the right device, port or cable (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Turtle Cove Tours is expanding its network. Each question needs you to apply a configuration rule to a new situation.</p>","items":[{"text":"The new store-room PC is 130 m from the switch. What is the BEST solution?","options":["Place another switch part-way so no copper run exceeds 100 m, or use fibre","Use a longer crossover cable","Connect the PC to the router's WAN port","Use one 130 m Cat6 cable"],"answer":0,"fb":"Copper Ethernet runs are limited to about 100 m."},{"text":"Which address should every PC use as its default gateway?","options":["The DNS server's address in Miami","The router's LAN address, such as 192.168.1.1","The printer's address","The ISP's public address"],"answer":1,"fb":"The router's LAN address is the door out of the LAN."},{"text":"The router has 4 LAN ports, but there are now 10 wired devices. What is the best design?","options":["Plug two devices into each port","Connect four devices and put the rest on the WAN port","Connect a 16-port switch to one router LAN port, and the devices to the switch","Use a bus with terminators"],"answer":2,"fb":"A switch extends the star through one router LAN port."},{"text":"The PCs use 192.168.1.x with mask 255.255.255.0, but someone set the printer manually to 192.168.2.50. What happens?","options":["The printer becomes the default gateway","It works normally","Only the DNS stops working","The PCs cannot reach the printer directly, because it is on a different network"],"answer":3,"fb":"With that mask, devices must share the first three numbers to be on the same network."},{"text":"Cables must run past the bakery's ovens and mixers. Which twisted-pair cable is the better choice?","options":["A USB cable","Cat5e","Cat6, which is better shielded against interference","Any cable, as interference does not affect copper"],"answer":2,"fb":"Cat6 is better shielded than Cat5e against electrical interference."},{"text":"The ISP says the connection type is PPPoE. Where is this entered?","options":["In the guest SSID settings","In the router's WAN settings, with the username and password the ISP supplied","On the hub","In each PC's DNS settings"],"answer":1,"fb":"The WAN connection type is configured on the router's WAN side."}],"win":"Well applied. Distance limits, the default gateway, extending a star with a switch, address ranges, cable shielding and WAN settings are the details that make a configuration answer precise."}
