     "up": {"title":"Firewall or other wired measure? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The clinic's technician has added more measures. Sort each by whether it is the router's hardware firewall, a host's software firewall, or another wired security measure.</p>","main":"What kind of security measure is this?","bins":["Hardware (router) firewall","Software (host) firewall","Other wired security measure"],"items":[{"t":"One gambling website is blocked for every clinic device at the router","bin":0,"fb":"A rule on the router's firewall applies to all devices behind it."},{"t":"The router lets inbound traffic through only when it is a reply to a request a staff device made","bin":0,"fb":"Filtering at the boundary for the whole LAN: hardware firewall."},{"t":"A managed switch shuts a port when an unknown MAC address appears","bin":2,"fb":"Port security on the switch."},{"t":"A rule blocks a remote-access program on the receptionist's PC only","bin":1,"fb":"A rule for one program on one computer: software firewall."},{"t":"The router's admin page can be reached only from inside the LAN","bin":0,"fb":"Blocking WAN access to management is part of configuring the router's firewall."},{"t":"Patch cables run inside locked trunking","bin":2,"fb":"Physical protection of cables."},{"t":"Only the practice manager holds the key to the network cabinet","bin":2,"fb":"Physical access control."},{"t":"Each staff PC's own firewall blocks inbound connections from other LAN devices except the records program","bin":1,"fb":"Host firewalls protect a device even from inside the LAN."},{"t":"A laptop switches to the Public profile on hotel Wi-Fi, blocking file sharing","bin":1,"fb":"Profiles are part of the laptop's own software firewall."},{"t":"The router's firmware is updated","bin":2,"fb":"Patching the router's own software closes known weaknesses."}],"win":"Well sorted. The router's firewall guards the boundary for every device, host firewalls guard individual computers even from inside the LAN, and physical, port and firmware measures add further layers."}
