     "up": {"title":"Troubleshoot in a logical order (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>A student's laptop at Carmichael Learning Centre is connected to the Wi-Fi but is very slow and cannot open websites by name. Put the nine troubleshooting steps in a logical order.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Find out whether other wireless devices in the room are affected, and whether anything has changed."},{"t":"Check that Wi-Fi is on, airplane mode is off and the laptop has joined the correct SSID."},{"t":"Check the signal strength and move closer to the access point."},{"t":"Run ipconfig to check the IP address, default gateway and DNS server."},{"t":"Ping the default gateway."},{"t":"Ping a public IP address such as 8.8.8.8."},{"t":"Run nslookup on a website name to test DNS."},{"t":"Run a speed test on the Wi-Fi and on a cabled laptop, and compare the results."},{"t":"Apply the fix, retest and record the fault and the solution."}],"win":"Logical and efficient: scope, wireless basics, signal, addressing, outward pings, DNS, performance comparison, then fix and document."}
