     "up": {"title":"Which upgrade helps? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"A clinic in Belize City runs imaging software on a PC with an SSD and 16 GB of RAM. Task Manager shows the processor at 100 per cent throughout each scan, memory at 40 per cent, and very little disk activity. Which upgrade is MOST likely to improve performance?","options":[{"t":"A larger SSD","fb":"The disk is barely busy; storage is not the limit."},{"t":"A faster Internet connection","fb":"The scans are processed locally, so the network is not involved."},{"t":"More RAM","fb":"Memory is only 40 per cent used and there is little disk activity, so there is no swapping to cure."},{"t":"A faster processor with more cores","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The CPU is at its limit while RAM and storage wait, so the processor is the bottleneck."}]}
