     "up": {"title":"Match the trade-off to the example (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Match each idea to the situation that shows it. The situations come from organisations across the region.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Flexibility versus optimisation","r":"A cross-platform app runs everywhere, but plays video less smoothly than a version written for one phone model"},{"l":"Hardware portability trade-off","r":"The lightest laptop has a smaller battery and RAM that cannot be upgraded"},{"l":"Replace faulty parts","r":"Only the failed hard disk in the clinic server is swapped; everything else is kept"},{"l":"Prevent breakdowns","r":"Dust filters are cleaned before the dry season and UPS batteries are tested every month"},{"l":"Cope with change","r":"The payroll package is updated when the tax rules change"},{"l":"Trained maintainers","r":"A network engineer on staff traces faults without calling an off-island contractor"},{"l":"Manuals","r":"Technical documentation lets a newly hired technician understand the server's set-up"},{"l":"Support equipment","r":"A cable tester, a spare switch and a test machine are kept in the IT room"},{"l":"Sequential versus direct access","r":"The tape archive must be wound through, while the disk jumps straight to a record"}],"win":"Well matched. Portability trades optimisation for flexibility, maintenance replaces, prevents and adapts with the support of people, manuals and equipment, and storage choices depend on access mode."}
