     "up": {"title":"Comparing storage for a business (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Dominica Craft Co-op keeps 2 TB of product photos on one office hard disk. The manager wants faster access, wants the photos to survive a hurricane, and has heard that ransomware can encrypt files and then the encrypted versions sync to the cloud. Which plan BEST meets all three needs?","options":[{"t":"Move working files to an SSD, keep a cloud backup with version history, and make a monthly offline copy stored off-site","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The SSD gives speed; version history lets earlier, clean copies be restored; the offline copy is beyond ransomware's reach; both copies are off-site."},{"t":"Mirror the photos onto a second hard disk in the same PC","fb":"This protects against one disk failing, but both disks are lost with the building or encrypted together."},{"t":"Move working files to an SSD and keep a synchronised cloud folder","fb":"Faster and off-site, but if ransomware encrypts the files, the synchronised copies may be encrypted too."},{"t":"Add more RAM to the office PC","fb":"RAM is volatile and protects no data."}]}
