     "title": "Configure a network from a design",
     "genre": "Paper 02 structured response: configuring a simple network",
     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">The Sunrise Bakery on Robb Street, Georgetown, has a network design showing: a star topology; a router connected to the ISP's fibre terminal; a hub connecting the manager's PC, the cash register PC and a printer; staff Wi-Fi for two tablets; and Wi-Fi for customers in the seating area. The owner, Mrs. Richardson, has just unpacked the router. Its label shows the default login admin / password.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Describe how the devices should be <b>physically connected</b> to match the design, naming the ports used. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Describe <b>FOUR</b> settings you would configure on the router to set up and secure the wireless networks. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>Explain <b>TWO</b> ways to secure the wired part of the network, including the role of the firewall. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Give <b>ONE</b> reason a star topology was chosen rather than a bus. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[15 marks]</b></p>",
     "min": 220,
     "max": 420,
     "frame": "<p><b>(a)</b> First, connect the fibre terminal to the router's ... port using ... Then connect the hub to ... Each PC and the printer is connected to ...<br><b>(b)</b> I would change the router password because ... I would set the SSID to ... I would choose WPA3 with AES because ... I would set a network key that ... For customers I would ...<br><b>(c)</b> The firewall ... Also, ...<br><b>(d)</b> A star was chosen because ... whereas in a bus ...</p>",
     "checklist": [
      "I named the WAN port for the ISP line and LAN ports for the hub and devices.",
      "I changed the default router password and explained why.",
      "I named WPA3 (or WPA2/WPA3), AES and a strong network key.",
      "I set a separate, isolated guest SSID for customers.",
      "I explained what the firewall does and one other wired security measure.",
      "I compared star with bus on the same feature."
     ],
