     "up": {"title":"Which part of access control? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These events from across the region are harder to place. Decide which of the four parts of access control each one shows. Watch especially for the difference between identifying and authenticating with a biometric.</p>","main":"Which part of access control is this?","bins":["Authorisation","Identification","Authentication","Accountability"],"items":[{"t":"The IT officer sets a rule that interns may read member files but not edit them","bin":0,"fb":"Defining permitted operations in advance: authorisation."},{"t":"When a nurse moves from the ward to the laboratory, her rights are changed to match her new role","bin":0,"fb":"Deciding what an identity may use is authorisation, updated when roles change."},{"t":"A door reader compares a fingerprint with every enrolled template to find out who is there","bin":1,"fb":"Answering \"who is this?\" by searching all templates: identification."},{"t":"Each change to a record is stamped with a user ID and time, so an auditor can trace a disputed loan","bin":3,"fb":"Tracing actions to an individual: accountability."},{"t":"A visitor tells the guard his name, and the guard finds it on the visitor list","bin":1,"fb":"Stating who you are is identification."},{"t":"Because each teller has a unique log-in, management can show which one approved an over-limit withdrawal","bin":3,"fb":"Unique IDs make actions traceable: accountability."},{"t":"A fingerprint is compared with the one template belonging to the user ID just typed","bin":2,"fb":"A one-to-one check of a claimed identity: authentication."},{"t":"A smart card scanned at the barrier tells the system which employee is arriving","bin":1,"fb":"The card supplies an identity: identification."},{"t":"The system compares the code on a teller's hardware token with the code it expects","bin":2,"fb":"Verifying a claimed identity with something she has: authentication."}],"win":"Precise sorting. Authorisation is defined in advance; identification claims an identity (and a biometric searching all templates identifies); authentication verifies a claim (a one-to-one check); accountability traces actions afterwards."}
