     "up": {"title":"Who changed the price? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"At Sunrise Hardware in Antriol, all six cashiers share the till account \"till1\", and nobody can tell who entered a heavily discounted price. The owner considers four fixes. Which one MOST directly restores accountability?","options":[{"t":"Give each cashier a unique user ID and password, and keep the till's audit log","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Unique identities let the audit log trace every price change to one person, which is accountability."},{"t":"Change the shared password every week","fb":"A new password for a shared account still cannot tell the cashiers apart."},{"t":"Install a CCTV camera above the till","fb":"It may help as evidence, but footage may not show who typed the price, and it does not link actions to accounts in the system."},{"t":"Encrypt the sales database","fb":"Encryption keeps data unreadable to outsiders; it does not record who made a change."}]}
