     "up": {"title":"Know, have or are? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These methods are less familiar. Sort each into the authentication factor it really relies on.</p>","main":"Which authentication factor is this?","bins":["Knowledge: something you know","Ownership: something you have","Characteristics: something you are"],"items":[{"t":"Hand geometry measured at a factory clock","bin":2,"fb":"A physical characteristic."},{"t":"A digital certificate stored on a company laptop","bin":1,"fb":"The certificate is held by the device: ownership."},{"t":"The chip on a bank card","bin":1,"fb":"The card is something you have."},{"t":"The iris pattern read at a laboratory door","bin":2,"fb":"A physical characteristic."},{"t":"A hardware token that shows a new six-digit code every minute","bin":1,"fb":"A device you carry: ownership."},{"t":"A memorised passphrase","bin":0,"fb":"Knowledge."},{"t":"Your mother's maiden name, given as a security answer","bin":0,"fb":"A fact you know."},{"t":"A one-time code shown by an authenticator app on your phone","bin":1,"fb":"It proves you hold the phone: ownership."},{"t":"The pattern you draw to unlock a phone","bin":0,"fb":"A remembered pattern is a knowledge factor."},{"t":"Your typing rhythm, checked as you enter your password","bin":2,"fb":"Keystroke dynamics is a behavioural characteristic."}],"win":"Well done. Codes, certificates, tokens and cards are things you have; patterns, answers and passphrases are things you know; typing rhythm, hand shape and iris are things you are."}
