     "up": {"title":"Getting into the payroll system (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Mrs. Richardson, the payroll officer at Market Street Trading Company, updates staff salaries. Put all nine security stages in order, from the street to that night's backup.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"She shows her staff ID badge to the security guard at the entrance."},{"t":"She presents her key card and enters a PIN to open the accounts office."},{"t":"She types her user ID at the payroll PC (identification)."},{"t":"She enters her password (something she knows)."},{"t":"She enters the code sent to her phone (something she has), completing authentication."},{"t":"The system grants read and write rights to salary records only (authorisation defined in advance)."},{"t":"She updates the salaries, and each change is written to the audit trail under her user ID (accountability)."},{"t":"She steps away, and the screen locks automatically after five idle minutes."},{"t":"That night, an encrypted backup of the payroll data is copied off-site."}],"win":"Exactly right. Physical layers come first, then identification, two-factor authentication, pre-defined authorisation and accountability, with screen locks and encrypted off-site backups adding further layers."}
