     "up": {"title":"Is it really two-factor? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Anguilla Island Bank's online banking currently asks for a password followed by a security question about the customer's first school. Which ONE change would MOST improve its authentication?","options":[{"t":"Replace the security question with a one-time code sent to the customer's registered phone","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Knowledge plus ownership is true two-factor authentication; a stolen password alone is no longer enough."},{"t":"Add a second security question","fb":"Three knowledge factors are still one factor, and school names are often findable on social media."},{"t":"Ask for a four-digit PIN as well as the password","fb":"A PIN is another knowledge factor, so this remains single-factor."},{"t":"Require customers to change their password every week","fb":"This is still a single factor, and frequent forced changes lead to weak, predictable passwords."}]}
