     "up": {"title":"Security terms (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Match each security term to the example that illustrates it. Two new terms have been added.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Data security","r":"A clinic keeps outsiders from reading or deleting patient files"},{"l":"Password","r":"The oldest, most common and weakest authentication method"},{"l":"Passphrase","r":"Longer than a password and usually made of several words"},{"l":"Authentication","r":"A teller proves she really is TELLER07"},{"l":"Authorisation","r":"Tellers may record deposits but may not approve loans"},{"l":"Accountability","r":"An auditor traces a disputed change to one user ID"},{"l":"Encryption","r":"Card details become ciphertext on their way to the bank"},{"l":"Data corruption","r":"A file saved during a power cut will not open"},{"l":"Data integrity","r":"Stock figures that are accurate, complete and consistent"},{"l":"Access control","r":"Regulates who or what can view or use resources in a computing environment"}],"win":"Excellent. Being able to match each term to a concrete example is what turns a definition into a two-mark explanation."}
