     "up": {"title":"Security or integrity? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"At Statia Fuel Depot, two problems occurred in one month. First, an intruder used a weak password to log in and deleted a week of delivery records. Second, authorised clerks entered several delivery quantities with an extra zero. Which statement correctly classifies BOTH problems?","options":[{"t":"Both are data integrity failures, because the records are now wrong","fb":"The second is integrity, but the first was unauthorised access and deletion, which is a data security failure."},{"t":"The deletion is data corruption; the extra zeros are a security failure","fb":"Corruption is accidental alteration; the deletion was deliberate. The zeros were entered by authorised staff, so security was not breached."},{"t":"The deletion is a data security failure; the extra zeros are a data integrity failure","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Security protects against unauthorised access and deletion; integrity concerns the accuracy of data entered by authorised users."},{"t":"Both are authentication failures","fb":"The clerks authenticated correctly; only the intruder's entry involved weak authentication."}]}
