     "up": {"title":"Hypertext and hyperlinks quick-fire (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Dante's study group is tackling harder questions about why hypertext and the web work as they do.</p>","items":[{"text":"Which statement BEST explains why hypertext is non-linear?","options":["It is always stored on more than one server","The reader, not the author, chooses the order and selection of topics","It is read from the last page to the first","It contains pictures as well as text"],"answer":1,"fb":"Non-linear means the user decides the path through the information."},{"text":"The web was not the first hypertext system. Why did it succeed where others did not spread?","options":["It was the only one with text","It needed no browser","It was owned by one company","It was the first to be interconnected with the Internet's TCP/IP, so any connected document could link to any other"],"answer":3,"fb":"Connecting hypertext to the Internet let links cross every computer on the network."},{"text":"A help system on a school's offline computer links its topics, but only within that one machine. Compared with the web, it lacks...","options":["a home page","hyperlinks","text","interconnection across networks"],"answer":3,"fb":"It is hypertext, but not interconnected across the Internet."},{"text":"What makes the WWW special, according to the notes?","options":["It carries email","Its combination of hypertext and multimedia","It uses only one server","It is older than the Internet"],"answer":1,"fb":"Hypertext plus multimedia is the web's distinguishing combination."},{"text":"A visitor follows links from a page in Belize City to servers in Europe and the USA without ever seeing where they are. This shows that...","options":["the pages are on one server","hyperlinks only work locally","the user only needs to know how to activate a link, not where the document is stored","all pages are copied to her phone first"],"answer":2,"fb":"Location is largely unseen in a hypertext structure."},{"text":"A link jumps to the \"Beaches\" heading further down the same page. This link points to...","options":["another place in the same document","a different document on the same server","another web site","a plug-in"],"answer":0,"fb":"Hyperlinks can target a place in the same document."},{"text":"Which pair is correctly distinguished?","options":["They mean exactly the same thing","Hypertext is the clickable element; a hyperlink is the way information is organised","Hypertext is the non-linear organisation of information; a hyperlink is the element that makes the jump","Both are types of browser"],"answer":2,"fb":"Keep the organisation (hypertext) separate from the mechanism (hyperlink)."}],"win":"Excellent. You explained the web's success, its multimedia nature and location transparency, and kept hypertext and hyperlink distinct."}
