     "up": {"title":"Match the web term (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These descriptions are more searching. Match each web term to the statement that is true of it alone.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Internet","r":"Would still carry email and video calls even if every web server were switched off"},{"l":"World Wide Web","r":"A subset of the Internet's services, made of linked hypertext documents"},{"l":"Web browser","r":"Requests pages with HTTP and renders HTML; search engines are reached through it"},{"l":"Search engine","r":"A web site, visited with a browser, that finds pages matching keywords"},{"l":"Hyperlink","r":"Turns separate files into a web of connected documents"},{"l":"Web page","r":"A single document with its own URL"},{"l":"Web site","r":"Related pages under one domain name, usually managed by one organisation"},{"l":"Home page","r":"Loads when only the domain name is typed, like a table of contents"},{"l":"Web server","r":"Stores pages and makes them available to any device on the Internet"}],"win":"Well matched. You can separate the network from the service, the software from the site, and the page from the collection."}
