     "up": {"title":"Static or dynamic page? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Some of these pages change, but only because someone edits them. Decide whether each is static or dynamic.</p>","main":"Static or dynamic page?","bins":["Static page","Dynamic page"],"items":[{"t":"A school calendar typed as HTML and edited by hand each term","bin":0,"fb":"Hand-edited files are static between edits."},{"t":"A page showing the current exchange rate between US dollars and Aruban florins, read from a database on each visit","bin":1,"fb":"Built from live data at each request: dynamic."},{"t":"A live cricket scorecard","bin":1,"fb":"New data on each visit: dynamic."},{"t":"A page that greets each logged-in member by name","bin":1,"fb":"Personalised for each visitor: dynamic."},{"t":"A shop's \"Terms and conditions\" page","bin":0,"fb":"The same for every visitor: static."},{"t":"The results page after a search for \"ferry Saba\"","bin":1,"fb":"Generated from the visitor's input: dynamic."},{"t":"An \"About us\" page uploaded once and never changed","bin":0,"fb":"The same file every time: static."},{"t":"A hotel gallery page that the owner edits and re-uploads each season","bin":0,"fb":"It changes only when the author edits the file: static."},{"t":"A news front page that adds stories automatically as reporters publish them","bin":1,"fb":"Updated automatically as new data arrives: dynamic."}],"win":"Well sorted. A page that changes only when its author edits it is still static; a dynamic page is built or updated automatically for each request."}
