     "up": {"title":"Match the URL protocol (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These descriptions include each protocol's limits and present-day status. Match each URL prefix to its description.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"http:","r":"Serves pages without encryption, so modern browsers may label them \"Not secure\""},{"l":"https:","r":"Encrypts the session between browser and server, shown by a padlock"},{"l":"file:","r":"file:///C:/Users/Kiara/test.html opens a page from the local drive"},{"l":"ftp:","r":"Pointed to files on anonymous servers; built-in support has been removed from major browsers"},{"l":"mailto:","r":"Hands an address to the email program to open a new message"},{"l":"news:","r":"Pointed to a Usenet group where comments are organised by topic"},{"l":"telnet:","r":"Remote terminal sessions that send passwords unencrypted, largely replaced by SSH"}],"win":"Well matched. You know what each prefix tells the browser and why several are now rarely used."}
