     "up": {"title":"Tag quick-fire (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Aaliyah's Saba Hiking Club page needs careful coding. Choose the BEST answer each time.</p>","items":[{"text":"Which start tag correctly makes a paragraph red and centred?","options":["&lt;p color=\"red\" align=\"centre\"&gt;","&lt;p style=\"color = red, text-align = center\"&gt;","&lt;p style=\"color: red; text-align: center;\"&gt;","&lt;p style=\"colour: red; text-align: centre;\"&gt;"],"answer":2,"fb":"Property: value pairs, separated by semicolons, with the American spellings color and center."},{"text":"Why is the style ignored in &lt;h1 style=\"color red;\"&gt;?","options":["The semicolon is not allowed","h1 cannot be styled","The colon between the property and the value is missing","red is not a colour name"],"answer":2,"fb":"A missing colon is the most common reason a style is ignored."},{"text":"Which heading plan is correct for a page with sections and sub-sections?","options":["h6 for the main heading","Several h1 headings and no h2","Only paragraphs in bold","One h1 for the page, h2 for sections, h3 for sub-sections"],"answer":3,"fb":"Headings should follow the structure of the page in order."},{"text":"She types several blank lines in her code between two sentences, but they appear on one line. To start a new paragraph she must...","options":["add spaces","press Enter more times","use the title element","use a new p element"],"answer":3,"fb":"Browsers ignore extra line breaks in code; elements create the layout."},{"text":"What is the main limitation of inline styling on a large site?","options":["It makes pages load without text","It cannot change colours","The same style must be repeated on every element, so updates are slow","It only works on images"],"answer":2,"fb":"Each element carries its own style, so site-wide changes need many edits."},{"text":"Why should a password never be written in an HTML comment?","options":["Comments are deleted by the browser","Comments slow the page down","Comments are encrypted","Anyone can read comments by viewing the page source"],"answer":3,"fb":"Comments are hidden from the page but not from the source code."}],"win":"Excellent. You checked style syntax character by character, planned headings properly and understood the limits of inline styling and comments."}
