     "up": {"title":"Build the Bodden Town Youth Football page (Challenge)","bloom":"Create","intro":"<p>Bodden Town Youth Football Club's page now has more requirements. Each decision builds on the last, and one choice is only partly right.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p>You open a blank file. Which structure do you write first?</p>","choices":[{"t":"The DOCTYPE and html, with the club's main heading inside the head.","to":"bad1","fb":"Visible content such as headings belongs in the body, not the head."},{"t":"The DOCTYPE, then html containing a head with a title, and a body.","to":"n2","fb":"Good. Correct structure first."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p>The fixtures table has columns Date, Opponent and Venue, and a final row must say \"All home games at the Bodden Town field\" across the whole width. How do you build that final row?</p>","choices":[{"t":"A tr with one td that has rowspan=\"3\".","to":"ok1","fb":"rowspan stretches down rows, not across columns."},{"t":"A tr with one td that has colspan=\"3\".","to":"n3","fb":"Right. colspan stretches a cell across columns."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p>The main heading must be green and centred. Which code do you use?</p>","choices":[{"t":"&lt;h1 style=\"color: green; text-align: center;\"&gt;","to":"n4","fb":"Correct syntax and spellings."},{"t":"&lt;h1 style=\"colour: green; text-align: centre;\"&gt;","to":"bad2","fb":"British spellings are not valid property names or values, so the style is ignored."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p>Parents register players: name, ONE age group (U10, U12 or U14), and permission for photos. How do you build the form?</p>","choices":[{"t":"A form with method=\"post\" containing a labelled text box, three radio buttons sharing one name, a checkbox for photo permission and a submit button.","to":"n5","fb":"Excellent. Each control fits the shape of its answer, and post keeps details out of the URL."},{"t":"A form with method=\"get\" and checkboxes for the age groups.","to":"bad3","fb":"Checkboxes allow several age groups, and get exposes children's details in the URL."}]},"n5":{"text":"<p>The page must link to the club's own \"Training times\" page (training.html) and to the league's web site. What do you write?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Links using file:///C:/Users/Coach/site/training.html and the league's name in bold.","to":"bad4","fb":"A file: path works only on the coach's own computer, and bold text is not a link."},{"t":"A relative link to training.html, and an absolute link to the league's full URL with target=\"_blank\"; the logo img has alt text.","to":"good","fb":"Right. Relative links for your own pages, absolute for other sites, and an accessible logo."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Page launched.</b> The structure, table, styling, form and links all work for every visitor. You applied every part of SO 2.19 and justified each choice.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>Odd layout.</b> The message cell stretches downwards and the table looks broken, though the data is there. Try again with colspan.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Missing heading.</b> The heading is not displayed as page content. Try again and put visible content in the body.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>Unstyled heading.</b> The heading stays black and left-aligned. Try again with color and center.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Bad data.</b> Players are registered in several age groups, and their names appear in shared links. Try again with radio buttons and post.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad4":{"text":"<p><b>Broken links.</b> Visitors get errors for the training page, and cannot click through to the league. Try again with relative and absolute links.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
