      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> A web page is one single hypertext document with its own URL. An example is the pharmacy's refill page. A web site is a collection of related web pages under one domain name. An example is all of Seaside Pharmacy's pages at seasidepharmacy.ai.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> (i) The protocol is https://. (ii) The domain name is seasidepharmacy.ai (the www is a prefix, not part of the domain name). (iii) The file name is refills.html.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> HTML is used to display data, whereas XML is used to store and transport data.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> (i) The domain name goes in and the IP address comes out. (ii) This is done by the Domain Name System (DNS). (iii) The browser then sends an HTTP request to that IP address, and the server sends back the refill page.</p>",
      "genre": "Paper 02 structured response: the Internet as interconnected hypertext documents",
      "teacherTip": "<p>Dial-down tip: once students can do these short parts, ask them to join (d) into four ordered steps using \"first, next, then, finally\". That is the bridge to the full 6-mark answer.</p>"
