     "model": "<pre>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Hato Reading Club&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;!-- Header section: club name and welcome --&gt;\n  &lt;h1 style=\"text-align: center; color: darkblue;\"&gt;Hato Reading Club&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;img src=\"logo.png\" alt=\"Hato Reading Club logo\" width=\"150\"&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Welcome! We meet &lt;b&gt;every Saturday&lt;/b&gt; at 10 a.m. to share great books.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Our next three books&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;ol&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Book one&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Book two&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Book three&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ol&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Meeting dates&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;table border=\"1\"&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Date&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Book&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Venue&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;7 November&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Book one&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Community centre&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;14 November&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Book two&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Community centre&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Join the club&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;form action=\"join.php\" method=\"post\"&gt;\n    &lt;label for=\"mname\"&gt;Name:&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"text\" id=\"mname\" name=\"mname\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"radio\" name=\"member\" value=\"adult\"&gt; Adult\n    &lt;input type=\"radio\" name=\"member\" value=\"teen\"&gt; Teen&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"submit\" value=\"Sign up\"&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n\n  &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.example.org/library\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Visit the public library&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</pre>",
     "teacherTip": "<p>Handwritten HTML is marked line by line. Examiners award a mark for each correct, complete element, so close every tag, keep attributes inside start tags with values in quotation marks, and spell style properties the American way (color, center). Indent nested elements: it shows structure and helps you spot an unclosed tag before the examiner does.</p>",
